<title>UK: Kingfisher eyeing French DIY alliance - paper.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher eyeing French DIY alliance - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Kingfisher Plc is considering a major move into the French DIY industry with the possible purchase of a stake in one of France's two largest DIY retailers, said the Observer newspaper on Sunday.</p>
<p>The report said the potential French DIY retailers are Castorama Dubois Investissements and Leroy Merlin, part of the Auchan group.</p>
<p>The Observer said that sources close to Kingfisher have suggested an alliance would be achieved by the company buying a minority stake to begin with rather than a full takeover.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
